{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"phantasmal-enhanced-barnowl","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nFifteen test files hand-build a nested pytest invocation (`[sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pytest\", ..., \"--basetemp\", ...]`); three were missing `--basetemp` and each became its own ticket (`grindable-deviant-angwantibo` in `tests/_store_isolation.py:32-48`, `acidic-ferreous-mole` in `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:838-857`, `asbestos-popular-tench` in `tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py` and siblings). Session log `kilted-centauric-cardinal` root-caused the store-isolation shutdown timeout in the same family.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `tests/_nested_pytest.py` with `run_nested_pytest(tmp_path, *args, timeout, env=None) -> CompletedProcess` that always passes `--basetemp`, `-p no:cacheprovider`, a bounded `timeout`, and `stdin=DEVNULL`; convert the fifteen sites. Guard: a meta-test asserts the literal `\"-m\", \"pytest\"` (and `\"-m pytest\"`) appears under `tests/` only in `_nested_pytest.py` (`# nested-pytest-ok:` escape for a test that must exercise the raw form).\n\n## Scope\n`tests/_nested_pytest.py` (new), `tests/_store_isolation.py`, `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`, `tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py`, the twelve other sites found by `grep -rln '\"-m\", \"pytest\"' tests/`, `tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_helper.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: the helper runs a one-test file and returns rc 0 with its basetemp under `tmp_path`. Edge: a hanging child is killed at `timeout` and reported with rc != 0 (no wall-clock assertion; a hang guard marked `# timing: hang-guard`). Pinning: every converted test file passes unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `grep -rn '\"-m\", \"pytest\"' tests/ | grep -v _nested_pytest.py` is empty; checked by the grep and the meta-test.\n- [ ] Every nested run's basetemp is under the caller's `tmp_path`; checked by the helper test inspecting the child's `--basetemp`.\n- [ ] The fifteen converted files pass in the default `Verified` tier under `-n 4`; checked by CI.\n","id":"25b4-34a3-09a2-4beb","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","priority":2,"tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"run_nested_pytest helper that always passes --basetemp, with a meta-test"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787352420262685001,"uuid":"a240c618-7d6a-458d-8913-b6da737dfcea"}